  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5084",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to GI-1 through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N interacts with Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and this compound further targets GI-1. Similarly, Mollicellin N also interacts with A704, which is a target of the same compound, reinforcing the connection between Mollicellin N and GI-1. Additionally, Mollicellin N is linked to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a different compound that also leads to GI-1. These findings collectively indicate that Mollicellin N exerts its biological effects through a variety of molecular mechanisms, all of which ultimately converge on GI-1. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, suggesting that GI-1 may be a downstream effector in the signaling cascade initiated by Mollicellin N.",
